## REST API Design Principles

The Laundry App backend follows RESTful architecture principles with a resource-oriented design:

- **Resource-Based URLs**: URLs represent resources (nouns), not actions (verbs)
- **HTTP Methods**: Use appropriate HTTP methods for operations (GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE)
- **Stateless**: Each request contains all necessary information; no server-side session state
- **Consistent Naming**: Use plural nouns for collections, lowercase with hyphens for readability
- **Versioning**: Include API version in the URL path (`/api/v1/`)
- **Standard Status Codes**: Use appropriate HTTP status codes for different scenarios
- **JSON Format**: All requests and responses use JSON format
- **HATEOAS**: Include relevant links in responses where applicable (optional)

## API Endpoint Structure

### URL Pattern
```
/api/v{version}/{resource}[/{id}][/{sub-resource}]
```

### Examples
```
GET    /api/v1/orders              # List all orders
GET    /api/v1/orders/:orderId     # Get single order
POST   /api/v1/orders              # Create new order
PUT    /api/v1/orders/:orderId     # Update entire order
PATCH  /api/v1/orders/:orderId     # Partial update
DELETE /api/v1/orders/:orderId     # Delete order

GET    /api/v1/orders/:orderId/items           # Get order items (sub-resource)
POST   /api/v1/orders/:orderId/cancel          # Action on resource
GET    /api/v1/customers/:customerId/orders    # Related resources
```

## HTTP Methods and Semantics

### GET - Retrieve Resources
- **Purpose**: Fetch one or multiple resources
- **Idempotent**: Yes
- **Safe**: Yes (no side effects)
- **Response**: 200 OK with resource data

```javascript
// GET /api/v1/orders/:orderId
router.get('/orders/:orderId', authenticateJWT, async (req, res, next) => {
  try {
    const order = await orderService.getOrderById(req.params.orderId);
    res.json({
      success: true,
      data: order
    });
  } catch (error) {
    next(error);
  }
});
```

### POST - Create Resources
- **Purpose**: Create new resources
- **Idempotent**: No
- **Safe**: No
- **Response**: 201 Created with created resource and Location header

```javascript
// POST /api/v1/orders
router.post('/orders', 
  authenticateJWT,
  validate(orderCreationSchema),
  async (req, res, next) => {
    try {
      const order = await orderService.createOrder(req.user.id, req.body);
      res.status(201)
        .location(`/api/v1/orders/${order.order_id}`)
        .json({
          success: true,
          data: order,
          message: 'Order created successfully'
        });
    } catch (error) {
      next(error);
    }
  }
);
```

### PUT - Replace Resources
- **Purpose**: Replace entire resource
- **Idempotent**: Yes
- **Safe**: No
- **Response**: 200 OK with updated resource

```javascript
// PUT /api/v1/customers/:customerId
router.put('/customers/:customerId',
  authenticateJWT,
  authorize('customer', 'admin'),
  validate(customerUpdateSchema),
  async (req, res, next) => {
    try {
      const customer = await customerService.updateCustomer(
        req.params.customerId,
        req.body
      );
      res.json({
        success: true,
        data: customer,
        message: 'Customer updated successfully'
      });
    } catch (error) {
      next(error);
    }
  }
);
```

### PATCH - Partial Update
- **Purpose**: Update specific fields of a resource
- **Idempotent**: Yes
- **Safe**: No
- **Response**: 200 OK with updated resource

```javascript
// PATCH /api/v1/orders/:orderId/status
router.patch('/orders/:orderId/status',
  authenticateJWT,
  authorize('admin', 'staff'),
  validate(statusUpdateSchema),
  async (req, res, next) => {
    try {
      const order = await orderService.updateOrderStatus(
        req.params.orderId,
        req.body.status
      );
      res.json({
        success: true,
        data: order,
        message: 'Order status updated'
      });
    } catch (error) {
      next(error);
    }
  }
);
```

### DELETE - Remove Resources
- **Purpose**: Delete a resource
- **Idempotent**: Yes
- **Safe**: No
- **Response**: 204 No Content or 200 OK with deletion confirmation

```javascript
// DELETE /api/v1/service-categories/:categoryId
router.delete('/service-categories/:categoryId',
  authenticateJWT,
  authorize('admin'),
  async (req, res, next) => {
    try {
      await serviceCatalogService.deleteCategory(req.params.categoryId);
      res.status(204).send();
    } catch (error) {
      next(error);
    }
  }
);
```

## HTTP Status Codes

### Success Codes (2xx)
- **200 OK**: Request succeeded, response includes data
- **201 Created**: Resource created successfully, include Location header
- **204 No Content**: Request succeeded, no response body needed (typically DELETE)

### Client Error Codes (4xx)
- **400 Bad Request**: Invalid request syntax or validation failure
- **401 Unauthorized**: Authentication required or failed
- **403 Forbidden**: Authenticated but insufficient permissions
- **404 Not Found**: Resource not found
- **409 Conflict**: Request conflicts with current state (e.g., duplicate email)
- **422 Unprocessable Entity**: Validation errors with detailed field errors
- **429 Too Many Requests**: Rate limit exceeded

### Server Error Codes (5xx)
- **500 Internal Server Error**: Unexpected server error
- **503 Service Unavailable**: Server temporarily unavailable (maintenance, overload)

